1	// Cold Email Engine — LEAD-DATABASE bulk import + continuous ingestion core.
2	//
3	// PURE ORCHESTRATION over an injected `LeadStore` so the exact same idempotent
4	// dedup/ingest logic runs from (a) the admin server action, (b) the operator CLI
5	// script scripts/import-leads.ts, and (c) the tests (with an in-memory store, no
6	// DB). The store is the ONLY thing that touches Prisma.
7	//
8	// IDEMPOTENCY + HYGIENE GUARANTEES:
9	//   - Dedup by NORMALIZED email (primary key of a lead). A repeat of an email
10	//     already seen earlier in the same file is skipped (skippedDup).
11	//   - An incoming email that matches an existing contact UPDATES it (fills blanks,
12	//     re-adds to the target list) — never inserts a duplicate. So a re-import of
13	//     the same file inserts 0.
14	//   - An incoming email that matches an existing DEAD or globally-SUPPRESSED
15	//     contact is NOT resurrected (skippedDead) — no update, no re-add to a list.
16	//   - A brand-new email that is already on the global suppression list is refused
17	//     (skippedDead) — we never add a suppressed address.
18	//   - Secondary signal: phone/website(domain) are recorded on the Business but the
19	//     dedup key is always the email (the only reliable per-person identifier).
20	
